            <ArticleTitle>[St. George's Hospital questionnaire (St. George's Respiratory Questionnaire) as an instrument for quality of life assessment in respiratory tract diseases].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>401-12</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>St. George's Respiratory Questionnaire (SGRQ) is one of the main measures of the quality of life in patients with pulmonary diseases. We review the literature concentrating the use of SGRQ in patients with asthma, chronic obstructive pulmonary disease, bronchectases, interstitial lung disease and in adult respiratory distress syndrome (ARSD).</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
